Later in the afternoon, I am back in my apartment.
I am a little tired after my shopping trip.
I sit on the bed and unpack my bags.
First, I take out my new, light green spring jacket.
Then I take out the blue cotton shirt.
I am looking forward to trying it on.
I take off my old sweater and put the shirt on.
But I can immediately feel a problem.
The shirt is way too small.
It is very tight across the shoulders.
I actually can barely lift my arms.
I look at myself in the mirror.
I obviously need a bigger size.
This model is much smaller than my normal size.
It is a bit of a pity that I did not try it on in the store.
But the line for the fitting rooms was simply too long.
I take the small shirt off again.
I fold it neatly and put it back in the bag.
Fortunately, I still have my receipt.
I can exchange the shirt for a bigger one when I get off work on Monday.
